A legacy :ERROR handler whose body holds a nested block. fmt.indent_style
says the scope-based :ERROR indents its body and every enclosing block
adds one level, so the :IF inside the handler should close at the
handler-body depth and the statement after it should stay in the body.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Recover;
:DECLARE x;
x := 0;
:ERROR;
x := 1;
:IF x > 0;
x := 2;
:ENDIF;
x := 3;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Recover;
	:DECLARE x;
	x := 0;
	:ERROR;
		x := 1;
		:IF x > 0;
			x := 2;
		:ENDIF;
		x := 3;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:1-4:7 warning deprecated_keyword: ':ERROR' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:1-4:7 warning deprecated_keyword: ':ERROR' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
